WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.020
Like a fairy tale

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.440
It's a sign the story has reached its end

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.360
Like a single passage taken from

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.980
A journey that was too long

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.320
Of the evil that once cast a shadow

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.660
Across this land

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.990
And the memories of the short journey

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.450
With the hero who defeated it

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:29.210
Beyond Journey's End

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.760
The story ends

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.260
And the hero goes to sleep

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.090
Leaving this land with

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.760
Days of peace and quiet

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.270
The passage of time heartlessly

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.430
Makes people forget

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.230
Even the tracks left behind by his life

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.020
Begin to rust

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.860
Just the same

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.150
Your words and wishes and courage

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.490
Are still inside of me

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.360
And they live on

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.910
We chose the same path

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.040
That's all it was supposed to be

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.580
Why is it that at some point

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.830
I wanted to understand the reason for

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.210
The tears that fall down my cheeks

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.290
Even now

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.670
If I retrace the journey we walked together

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.220
Even though you're not there

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.890
I know I'll be able to find it

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:38.740
Long-range magic is a combination of 
three key factors essential to mages.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.240
There's the amount of mana,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.330
the strength with which it's fired, and the 
level of control the mage has over it.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.330
You know that much, don't you?

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.120
Yes.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.920
Earlier, your magic dissipated 
before it reached its target.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.760
That's a sign that your mana 
and firing strength are lacking.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:59.390
It's not something you can fix overnight.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:03.510
Regardless of your talent, 
it'll take years to master.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:13.230
However, your level of control 
over the magic is very high.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.610
That's what most people 
tend to have trouble with.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.110
But you've got no problems there,

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.610
so just be patient with yourself.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:23.950
Okay.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.820
Is Fern's training coming along smoothly?

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.150
In just four years, she's learned more 
than most people do in ten.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.780
She's studying too hard. 
It's not a good thing.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.330
She's been spending all her 
time in the woods lately.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.040
She must really love magic.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.960
But she's still a long way 
from becoming a proper mage.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.250
I'll finish deciphering the 
grimoire before she does.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.590
I see.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.970
Say, Heiter.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.930
This grimoire probably...

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.230
Heiter?

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.440
Don't look at me like that.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.910
If anything, it's a miracle 
I've been mobile until now.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.330
I'll try to decipher the grimoire quickly.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.330
I'd appreciate that.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.090
Fern, put your training on hold.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.220
Heiter collapsed. 
I need you to stay with him.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.050
But I still haven't hit the rock.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.180
You'll do it eventually. Right now—

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.810
Eventually isn't good enough.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.570
Mr. Heiter will die before then.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.070
He saved my life.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.500
It'd be a waste for you to die now.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.050
A waste?

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:31.470
A long time ago, I lost an old friend.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:35.180
Unlike me, he was straight as an arrow,

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:39.310
and he never abandoned 
anyone who was in need.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:46.490
If he'd survived instead of me, 
he would've saved a lot of people.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:52.950
Since I'm not like him, I planned to 
live out the rest of my days quietly,

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.500
but one day, I suddenly realized something.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.750
If I died without doing anything,

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.460
all the courage, strength of will, 
and friendship I learned from him—

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:09.130
even all my precious memories—
would vanish from this world.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:16.890
If you have precious memories 
inside yourself as well,

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.480
then I think it'd be a waste for you to die.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:27.110
Mr. Heiter has always feared 
dying and leaving me alone.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.990
He did the right thing.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.240
I don't want him to regret saving me.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.250
I don't care if it's as a mage 
or whatever else—

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:42.000
learning some kind of skill to support 
myself is my way of repaying him.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:47.380
I want him to be glad he saved me 
and to know I'll be fine.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:54.260
You remember everything 
I've taught you, don't you?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.100
Yes.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.520
Then do as you like.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:02.120
It didn't contain any spells for bringing 
back the dead or granting immortality.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.750
I see.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.250
Did you know that already?

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:09.380
The fear of death is immeasurable.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:14.130
If such spells existed, 
Ewig would've cast them on himself.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.760
Then why?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.310
How is Fern?

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.850
She has room for improvement in some areas,

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.520
but it wouldn't be wrong 
to call her a proper mage.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.190
I see. Then she made it in time.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.990
Now she won't get in your way, Frieren.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.200
Will you bring her with you on your travels?

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.500
I'm sorry, Heiter. 
That's the one thing I can't do.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.250
She'd only get in my way.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.960
You tricked me, Heiter.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.300
Your payment for deciphering 
the grimoire is in the desk drawer.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.800
Please leave this place tonight.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.760
Why?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.390
As you can see, I don't have much longer.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:12.780
I don't want her to experience 
losing anyone else.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.780
Frieren, please look after Fern.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.790
Are you trying to put on 
a brave face again, Heiter?

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.710
Fern has been ready to say goodbye 
to you for some time now.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.250
What you need to do before your death

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.050
is give her a proper farewell

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.680
and make as many memories as you can.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:47.060
Frieren, you really are a kind girl.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.700
Why did you save Fern?

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.720
It's what Himmel the Hero would've done.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:23.600
You're right.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:41.450
Then maybe I'll do the same.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.290
Thank you.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:57.800
Because of you, I was able to 
repay my debt to Mr. Heiter.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.840
He just tricked me, is all.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.220
This corrupt priest.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.230
Shall we go, then?

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:18.000
Episode 2: It Didn't Have to Be Magic...

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:32.180
26 years after the death of Himmel the Hero,
in the Turk region located in the central lands

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:36.060
That's enough, Fern.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:37.470
We're finished.

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:43.310
Thank you for your help.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.900
Here's your reward.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.280
We've been doing such simple work.

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:52.320
That's how adventuring goes.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.870
What were we paid in?

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:58.830
Folk magic. It's a spell 
that produces warm tea.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.290
We'll try it out later.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:05.420
The other day we learned a spell 
for removing rust from bronze statues.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:10.380
Before that, we learned a spell 
for turning sweet grapes into sour ones.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:09.210
How is it?

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.300
Sour.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.720
You keep collecting the strangest spells.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.010
It's my hobby, after all.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:19.520
Ms. Frieren, you really do love magic.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:22.270
Only somewhat, like you.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.520
I feel like we're a little different.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.110
We're the same.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:33.110
Will you really do something for me?

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:38.410
Since I'm an herbalist, 
I don't have any spells to teach you.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:43.790
That's fine. Just learning about 
the local flora is helpful enough.

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:49.420
This is it.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.350
It's a statue of Himmel the Hero.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:59.810
It's in terrible shape, isn't it?

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:03.560
It's too much for one old woman to handle.

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:07.230
And the villagers don't care anymore.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.070
Run!

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:34.090
When the village was attacked by a monster,

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:36.550
Mr. Himmel fought valiantly to defend us.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:39.890
It saddens me to see him treated like this.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:46.850
No, it's what he deserves. 
It's Himmel's fault for wanting to show off.

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:51.780
When the villagers offered to make a statue 
of him, he should have just declined.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:54.740
Is this okay?

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:56.740
This pose isn't too handsome, is it?

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:58.990
Just hurry up and pick something.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:01.490
He drove the sculptor mad 
by spending 18 hours choosing a pose.

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:00.410
I'm hungry.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:06.460
In the end, they settled on 
a ridiculously plain one.

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:09.380
What a strange story.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:14.880
Come to think of it, there was an 
elven mage in the hero's party.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.510
Shall we get this cleaned up?

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.270
Thank you.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.060
Magic sure is amazing, isn't it?

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.520
There isn't a speck of rust left.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.530
I wish there was a bit more color, though.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.900
Perhaps I'll plant some flowers later.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:41.490
Ms. Frieren, you have a spell that 
produces a field of flowers, right?

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:44.870
You're right. I guess I could just 
conjure something up...

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:51.330
No, blue moon weed flowers would be best.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.000
What kind of flowers are those?

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.380
I don't know. I've never seen them.

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:57.510
Then why?

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:00.140
They grow in Himmel's hometown.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:03.350
But you can't conjure flowers 
you've never seen before.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.770
Blue moon weed...

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.230
Now that's a name I haven't 
heard in a long time.

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:21.780
Long ago, there used to be a 
field of them in those woods.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.660
They don't grow around here anymore?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.540
They all died out.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:37.170
It's been decades since they've 
been spotted in these lands.

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.220
I see.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.800
Let's go, Fern.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:45.810
Okay.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.020
You're hiding something.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.650
I won't be mad, so show me what it is.

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:02.570
They're seed rats. Pests that consume seeds.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:04.280
I'll release them in the woods.

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:12.040
Fern, shall we go look for blue moon weed?

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:14.170
Are you serious?

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:17.710
There was a field of them 
in these woods until recently.

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:19.010
That was decades ago.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.260
But they're worth looking for.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:28.100
If we find and analyze them, we can acquire 
a spell for conjuring blue moon weed flowers.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.600
For Mr. Himmel?

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.100
No...

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:34.770
I'm probably doing this for myself.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:33.330
Ms. Frieren, we've been searching for 
blue moon weed for six months now.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:37.580
You're right. Perhaps we should 
broaden our search area.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.470
Oh, I don't often see you on your own.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:56.690
It's been a while since you 
first came to the village.

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:00.610
Have you found any blue moon weed?

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.190
Do you think we'll find any?

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.740
Ms. Frieren's obsession with 
magic is extraordinary.

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:13.700
At this rate, she'll continue searching 
for years, if not decades.

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:19.170
She's a mage who possesses the 
power to save many people.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:25.340
She shouldn't spend her time searching 
for something that doesn't exist.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.510
You're so young.

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:33.180
Am I wrong?

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.850
I don't think so,

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:41.820
but Ms. Frieren must see things differently.

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:49.530
But since she's so much more 
mature than we are,

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:53.990
I'm sure she'd understand if you honestly 
conveyed those feelings to her.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:16.850
These are the seeds of a related species 
she kept for their medicinal properties.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:21.440
Could we plant these around 
Himmel's statue instead?

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:23.860
I get it, Fern.

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:26.400
I made you worry.

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:32.200
I'm not just spending my own time on this.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:33.990
It's time to go.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:37.000
I'll end my search soon.

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:42.130
How many years is soon?

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:43.920
Soon.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:47.460
You don't know when to stop—

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:00.690
Shall we follow it?

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:34.720
Ms. Frieren, why do you collect spells?

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.390
It's just a hobby of mine.

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:38.390
I find that hard to believe.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:41.390
It really is just a hobby.

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:45.770
I used to live much more apathetically.

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:12.420
Gross.

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:24.810
But then I got to know an idiot who 
complimented the spells I gathered.

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:26.600
That's all.

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:30.400
That's a silly reason.

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.320
You're right.

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:55.550
Is that...

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:57.340
It's a petal.

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:03.310
They say seed rats bury their food 
in safe places away from enemies.

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:05.890
They're clever animals, aren't they?

00:22:06.310 --> 00:22:07.730
I wouldn't say that.

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:13.150
Since they bury their food in so many places,
they often forget where.

00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:18.910
Blue moon weed?

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:23.410
It's a flower that grows in 
my homeland. It's beautiful.

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:26.830
Not as beautiful as me, though.

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:28.420
Shall we get going?

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:30.420
Frieren.

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:33.630
Someday, I'd like to show them to you.

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:35.670
I see.

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:37.630
If we have the opportunity, perhaps.

00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:49.730
I figured they'd be here, 
but I wasn't expecting so many.

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:56.820
It took longer than I would've liked, Himmel.

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:04.950
I can't believe we really found them.

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:08.160
Now we can create a spell for blue moon weed.

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.630
Why are you so passionate about magic?

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:13.710
I don't understand.

00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:15.960
But you do.

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:19.970
You never gave up on becoming a mage.

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:23.100
That's different.

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:28.180
I would've been happy to learn any skill 
that allowed me to support myself.

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:31.350
It didn't have to be magic...

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:35.230
But you chose magic.

00:23:47.580 --> 00:23:48.870
You're right.

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:55.710
I never thought I'd see blue moon weed again.

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:57.840
They're beautiful.

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:01.090
Thank you, Ms. Frieren.

00:24:01.550 --> 00:24:05.350
Now this statue will never be forgotten.

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:08.890
Oh, I nearly forgot.

00:24:10.230 --> 00:24:11.190
There.

00:24:12.310 --> 00:24:15.110
How cute.

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:17.360
Shall we go?

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:22.530
And you alright

00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:25.030
Can you hear me

00:24:25.830 --> 00:24:31.920
Trailing along deserted train tracks

00:24:31.920 --> 00:24:34.250
Crying excessively

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:37.420
Wanting you to smile

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:43.470
I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh

00:24:43.470 --> 00:24:47.180
There's something I'd like to tell you

00:24:47.180 --> 00:24:49.930
With words more precious than a goodbye

00:24:49.930 --> 00:24:55.610
Unremarkable yet special

00:24:55.610 --> 00:24:59.150
See, things that couldn't have been

00:24:59.150 --> 00:25:02.200
Seen if it weren't for these eyes

00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:06.950
Why? They begin to overflow

00:25:06.950 --> 00:25:13.040
So, if I were to be born again

00:25:13.040 --> 00:25:18.880
I would surely choose this place once more

